Subject: Cantor Schema Direction Constraint Ledger

@ [ledger_uuid] cb9a915a-c60e-4fcb-9e8b-46519f93ec9a

& [Must] is direction complete
  + tag every root document, definition universe, account, fingerprint, residual, and compatibility result with one direction
  + generate every definition in one universe using only its selected schemars contract
  + preserve local references inside that universe and prohibit cross-universe references
  + assign PreparedRunRequest an input identity and an output identity
  + normalize before digesting and use domain-separated contract fingerprints
  + compare compatibility only within equal directions
  + report cross-direction byte equality separately and without authorization meaning

& [MustNot] prevents conflation
  - never: key a global definition solely by type name
  - never: reuse a cached schema generated under the opposite contract
  - never: let equal bytes erase direction from identity or fingerprints
  - never: make bundle layout change local JSON Pointer meaning
  - never: claim direction-qualified schema proves serde behavior, semantic bounds, or authority

& [StopConditions] are exact
  + stop implementation if any emitted document lacks direction
  + stop if a local reference can resolve into the opposite universe
  + stop if PreparedRunRequest has only one contract account
  + stop if golden output changes without same-direction compatibility classification

